  "notes": "Official cause code and category are TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative attributes the failure to a 'most likely' latent insulation defect from a 2006 rewind, with possible contributing factors from 2019 refurbishment, storage, and testing that could not be conclusively determined due to fault-area destruction. Modeled as separate sequential FailureMode nodes per rule 5 (insulation defect -> turn-to-turn short -> ground/phase-to-phase short -> parallel breaker trip and motor overheating/failure -> pump trip -> prolonged inoperability/TS violation). Service Water Pump B is modeled as a Component (not System) since it is the specific standby pump manually started, not a separate system; BACKED_UP_BY edge reflects narrative statement it was started and restored loop pressure. No prior similar LERs were found per Section VI.B, so no SIMILAR_TO edge or stub LER node was created. IEEE 803/805 codes (MO, BI) taken directly from the 'NAME OF EACH COMPONENT OR SYSTEM' section."
